        <section class="c-page__body" id="maincontent">
            <section class="c-container c-container--has-bg-color u-pure-white-bg c-container--inset "
    id="details">

    
    <section class="c-container__blocks">

        <div class="o-layout o-layout--center">
                            <div class="o-layout__item u-2/3@desktop">
    <div class="c-col c-col-text-area u-transparent-bg" >
    	
        
                    <p class="lead-p c-drop-cap">M<strong>uch Ado About Nothing</strong> <span data-olk-copy-source="MessageBody">is &#8216;the Globe at its very best&#8217; </span>★★★★★ (<i>London Theatre</i>) in this &#8216;joyous… magical&#8217; ★★★★ (<i>The Telegraph</i>) production.</p>
<p><span data-olk-copy-source="MessageBody">The war is over, but the battle for love is just beginning – especially for Beatrice and Benedick. Shakespeare&#8217;s most incisive romantic comedy is &#8216;a delight on a summer&#8217;s evening&#8217; </span>★★★★ (<i>WhatsOnStage</i>) and &#8216;stylish&#8217; with &#8216;heaps of humour&#8217; ★★★★ (<i>The Standard</i>).</p>
<p><span data-olk-copy-source="MessageBody">Set in a sun-soaked world of reputation and status, <b>Chelsea Walker</b> (<i>All&#8217;s Well That Ends Well</i>, Sam Wanamaker Playhouse) directs &#8216;a sublime production… that captures the hearts and minds of its audience&#8217; </span>★★★★★ (<i>All That Dazzles</i>).</p>
<p><span data-olk-copy-source="MessageBody">Book your tickets for &#8216;a slick sitcom&#8217; (<i>The Times</i>) and</span> &#8216;a sure summer blockbuster… eminently worth seeing&#8217; (<i>The Guardian</i>).</p>
<blockquote>
<p class="lead-p">‘Therein do men from children nothing differ.’</p>
</blockquote>
<p><i class="fal fa-info-circle"></i><strong><span data-teams="true"> This production contains mild reference to illegal substances.</span> </strong><b data-olk-copy-source="MessageBody">Please contact the Ticketing team on 020 7401 9919 or </b><a id="OWA264380aa-6891-92c7-a090-a949dfc84c66" class="x_OWAAutoLink" title="mailto:tickets@shakespearesglobe.com" href="/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection#95e1fcf6fef0e1e6d5e6fdf4fef0e6e5f0f4e7f0e6f2f9faf7f0bbf6faf8" data-linkindex="0"><b><span class="__cf_email__" data-cfemail="23574a404846575063504b42484650534642514650444f4c41460d404c4e">[email&#160;protected]</span></b></a> <b>if you would like further details on the play’s content.</b></p>
            </div>
</div>
                            <div class="o-layout__item u-1/3@desktop">
    <div class="c-col c-col-text-area c-col--has-bg-color u-green-black-bg" >
    	
        
                    <p class="lead-p"><strong><i class="fal fa-info-circle"></i> DETAILS</strong></p>
<p><i class="fal fa-ticket"></i><strong> TICKETS</strong><br />
<strong> Galleries (Seating) </strong>£89–£29*<br />
*includes a £3 per order transaction fee and a £1 per ticket restoration levy</p>
<p><strong> Standing </strong>£10, £5 (Get two free standing tickets for one performance a year with <span role="presentation"><a id="OWAb863c6cf-715c-908c-577d-a91318287b54" class="OWAAutoLink" title="https://www.shakespearesglobe.com/join-and-support/membership/" href="https://www.shakespearesglobe.com/join-and-support/membership/" data-auth="NotApplicable"><u>Membership</u></a></span>)</p>
<p><i class="fal fa-map-marked"></i> This event is <strong>on-site</strong> in the <a href="https://www.shakespearesglobe.com/venue/globe-theatre/">Globe Theatre</a></p>
<p><i class="fal fa-clock"></i><strong> Running time</strong> 2 hours 30 minutes, including a 20 minute interval</p>
<p class="smaller-p"><strong><a href="https://www.shakespearesglobe.com/policies/terms-conditions/">Terms and conditions</a></strong><br />
<span data-teams="true">All under 16s must be accompanied by an adult, and cannot be sat separately.</span></p>
<p>Photography: Helen Murray<br />
Art Direction: Kharis Wong</p>
<p class="lead-p">Part of <a href="https://www.shakespearesglobe.com/discover/blogs-and-features/2026/01/26/imagine-together-2026/">Summer 2026</a></p>
            </div>
</div>
