                    				                                            <div class="o-layout__item c-col-bio-single">
                            <h3 class="c-col-bio__role u-h3">Composer</h3>
                                                            <a href="#0"
                                data-a11y-dialog-show="a11y-dialog"
                                data-dialog-title='Angus MacRae'
                                data-dialog-content='<p>Angus MacRae is a composer, multi-instrumentalist and recording artist whose work moves seamlessly between records, experimental live performance and scores for theatre, dance and film. His music resists easy categorisation, although it sits broadly at the intersection of classical and electronic music, with improvisation often at its heart.</p>
<br>
                                                                    <a href="https://www.shakespearesglobe.com/bio/angus-macrae/">View full biography</a>
                                '

                                                                    data-dialog-img='<figure class="c-col-bio__mugshot">
                                        <img
                                            src="https://images.shakespearesglobe.com/uploads/2025/12/Angus-theatre-headshot-aspect-ratio-1513-1507.jpg?resize=320%2C320&gravity"
                                            alt="Angus MacRae looks to the left of the camera. He stands in front of a dark background and wears glasses and a red check scarf around his neck."
                                            title="Angus-theatre-headshot-aspect-ratio-1513-1507">
                                    </figure>'
                                                                class="c-dialog--open c-link">
                                                                            <h4 class="c-col-bio__name u-h5">Angus MacRae</h4>
                                                                    </a>
                                                    </div>
                    				                                            <div class="o-layout__item c-col-bio-single">
                            <h3 class="c-col-bio__role u-h3">Costume Supervisor</h3>
                                                            <a href="#0"
                                data-a11y-dialog-show="a11y-dialog"
                                data-dialog-title='Jackie Orton '
                                data-dialog-content='<p><span data-contrast="auto">Previous work at Shakespeare’s Globe includes<em> A Midsummer Night&#8217;s Dream</em>, </span><i><span data-contrast="auto">Romeo and Juliet</span></i><span data-contrast="auto"> (2025 &amp; 2021), </span><i><span data-contrast="auto">Taming of the Shrew</span></i><span data-contrast="auto">, </span><i><span data-contrast="auto">Comedy of Errors</span></i><span data-contrast="auto">, </span><i><span data-contrast="auto">As You Like It</span></i><span data-contrast="auto">, </span><i><span data-contrast="auto">The Tempest</span></i><span data-contrast="auto">, </span><i><span data-contrast="auto">The Winter’s Tale</span></i><span data-contrast="auto">, </span><i><span data-contrast="auto">Hamlet</span></i><span data-contrast="auto">.</span><span data-ccp-props="{}"> </span></p>
<br>
                                                                    <a href="https://www.shakespearesglobe.com/bio/jackie-orton/">View full biography</a>
                                '

                                                                    data-dialog-img='<figure class="c-col-bio__mugshot">
